dropna: n=10 mean_ret=0.006005 n_ret_nonnull=9
ffill: n=12 mean_ret=0.004913 n_ret_nonnull=11
interpolate: n=12 mean_ret=0.004909 n_ret_nonnull=11
tradeoffs: dropna shortens the sample and changes overlapping windows; ffill invents flat prices on missing days (fake prints) using only PAST prints; time-interpolate(method='time') fills gaps using BOTH earlier AND later known prices (look-ahead) — never feed interpolated prices into signals; in backtests only ffill or dropping rows is allowed.

